{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"deddea00-dd46-4e28-94dd-95bbac73577b","step":{"id":"s1","script":"For positive x, represent x squared plus six x as a square and two rectangles, each with area three x.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Completing the square"},{"op":"equation","id":"start","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"x^2+6x=x^2+3x+3x"},{"op":"figure","id":"model","region":"right","frame":{"x":[-0.8,8],"y":[-0.8,8],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"polyline","id":"square","points":[[0,0],[4,0],[4,4],[0,4]],"closed":true},{"kind":"text","at":[2,2],"text":"x²"},{"kind":"measure","from":[0,-0.3],"to":[4,-0.3],"label":"x"},{"kind":"measure","from":[-0.3,0],"to":[-0.3,4],"label":"x"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"deddea00-dd46-4e28-94dd-95bbac73577b","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Place one three-by-x rectangle beside the square and the other above it. The outside almost forms a larger square.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"strips","on":"model","marks":[{"kind":"polyline","points":[[4,0],[7,0],[7,4],[4,4]],"closed":true,"fill":true},{"kind":"polyline","points":[[0,4],[4,4],[4,7],[0,7]],"closed":true,"fill":true},{"kind":"text","at":[5.5,2],"text":"3x"},{"kind":"text","at":[2,5.5],"text":"3x"},{"kind":"measure","from":[4,-0.3],"to":[7,-0.3],"label":"3"},{"kind":"measure","from":[-0.3,4],"to":[-0.3,7],"label":"3"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"deddea00-dd46-4e28-94dd-95bbac73577b","step":{"id":"s3","script":"The missing corner is three by three. Adding nine fills the gap and completes a square with side x plus three.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"corner","on":"model","marks":[{"kind":"polyline","id":"patch","points":[[4,4],[7,4],[7,7],[4,7]],"closed":true,"fill":true},{"kind":"text","at":[5.5,5.5],"text":"9"},{"kind":"measure","from":[0,7.5],"to":[7,7.5],"label":"x + 3"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"complete","anchor":{"el":"start","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"x^2+6x+9=(x+3)^2"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Why do we add nine rather than six to complete this square?","expected_gist":"Splitting 6x gives two strips of width 3, leaving a 3-by-3 corner with area 9."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"deddea00-dd46-4e28-94dd-95bbac73577b","step":{"id":"s4","script":"To keep the original expression unchanged, subtract the nine we added. Half the x coefficient, then square it: that gives the missing corner.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"result","anchor":{"el":"complete","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"x^2+6x=(x+3)^2-9"},{"op":"equation","id":"rule","anchor":{"el":"result","side":"below","gap":0.12},"latex":"\\text{Corner area}=\\left(\\frac{6}{2}\\right)^2=9"},{"op":"figure","id":"reminder","on":"model","marks":[{"kind":"text","at":[5.5,7.8],"text":"subtract corner","size":"small"},{"kind":"segment","from":[5.5,7.6],"to":[5.5,6.3],"arrow":true}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
